menu "EC-Cameras module"

    choice EC_FRAMESIZE
        prompt "Frame size"
        default EC_FRAMESIZE_XGA
        help
            XGA matches the Arduino sketch this module replaces. Dropping to
            SVGA or VGA is the cheapest way to cut bandwidth: three cameras at
            XGA share the same 2.4 GHz band as the measurement modules.

        config EC_FRAMESIZE_VGA
            bool "VGA 640x480"
        config EC_FRAMESIZE_SVGA
            bool "SVGA 800x600"
        config EC_FRAMESIZE_XGA
            bool "XGA 1024x768"
    endchoice

    config EC_JPEG_QUALITY
        int "JPEG quality (0 best, 63 worst)"
        range 0 63
        default 12
        help
            The sketch used 10. Slightly lower quality costs little visually and
            takes a noticeable bite out of the frame size.

    config EC_MAX_FPS
        int "Frame rate cap, 0 disables it"
        range 0 30
        default 10
        help
            The sketch streamed as fast as the sensor produced frames. At XGA
            that is several Mbit/s per camera with nobody watching the total.
            Capping is one vTaskDelay and makes the load predictable.

endmenu
